 "brief": "A pillow block in PETG (FDM, printed base down, layers along Z) that holds a 608 bearing (22 mm OD, 7 mm wide, 8 mm bore) for an 8 mm shaft running along X at height z = 20. The block bolts to a flat plate (the plane z = 0) with two M5 bolts and nuts at y = -24 and y = +24, through a 6 mm thick base. It stays inside x = -7 to 7, y = -32 to 32, z = 0 to 34. The bearing presses in from the -X side and sits against a shoulder. A belt on the shaft pulls the bearing up to 300 N down, up, or either way sideways (Y), and the shaft can push 60 N along X into the shoulder. Safety factor 2.5.",
